1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:01,900
Luke 4

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:07,100
And Jesus, full of the Holy Spirit, returned from the Jordan,

3
00:00:07,520 --> 00:00:10,640
and was led by the Spirit in the wilderness for forty days,

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,500
being tempted by the devil.

5
00:00:13,060 --> 00:00:15,240
And he ate nothing during those days,

6
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:17,980
and when they were ended, he was hungry.

7
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:20,360
The devil said to him,

8
00:00:21,160 --> 00:00:26,060
If you are the Son of God,

9
00:00:26,060 --> 00:00:31,060
command this stone to become bread.

10
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:33,800
And Jesus answered him,

11
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:38,040
It is written, Man shall not live by bread alone.

12
00:00:38,900 --> 00:00:43,800
And the devil took him up and showed him all the kingdoms of the world in a moment of time,

13
00:00:44,120 --> 00:00:45,240
and said to him,

14
00:00:46,500 --> 00:00:54,220
To you I will give all this authority and their glory,

15
00:00:54,220 --> 00:00:56,040
for it has been given to you.

16
00:00:56,060 --> 00:00:59,140
It has been delivered to me,

17
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:03,760
and I give it to whom I will.

18
00:01:04,980 --> 00:01:08,880
If you then will worship me,

19
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:13,660
it will all be yours.

20
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:16,780
And Jesus answered him,

21
00:01:17,460 --> 00:01:18,720
It is written,

22
00:01:19,300 --> 00:01:22,920
You shall worship the Lord your God, and him only shall you serve.

23
00:01:23,220 --> 00:01:25,040
And he took him to Jerusalem,

24
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:27,340
and set him on the pinnacle of the temple,

25
00:01:27,340 --> 00:01:28,620
and said to him,

26
00:01:29,900 --> 00:01:33,740
If you are the Son of God,

27
00:01:33,740 --> 00:01:36,940
throw yourself down from here,

28
00:01:36,940 --> 00:01:39,940
for it is written,

29
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:47,540
He will command his angels concerning you to guard you,

30
00:01:47,540 --> 00:01:52,280
and on their hands they will bear you up,

31
00:01:52,280 --> 00:01:54,840
lest you strike your foot.

32
00:01:54,840 --> 00:01:59,860
And Jesus answered him,

33
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:01,660
It is said,

34
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:04,820
You shall not put the Lord your God to the test.

35
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:07,760
And when the devil had ended every temptation,

36
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:11,180
he departed from him until an opportune time.

37
00:02:12,380 --> 00:02:15,780
And Jesus returned in the power of the Spirit to Galilee,

38
00:02:16,060 --> 00:02:19,440
and a report about him went out through all the surrounding country,

39
00:02:19,800 --> 00:02:23,920
and he taught in their synagogues, being glorified by all.

40
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:28,700
And he came to Nazareth, where he had been brought up.

41
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,340
And as was his custom,

42
00:02:31,740 --> 00:02:34,060
he went to the synagogue on the Sabbath day,

43
00:02:34,320 --> 00:02:35,720
and he stood up to read.

44
00:02:36,420 --> 00:02:39,460
And the scroll of the prophet Isaiah was given to him.

45
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,300
He unrolled the scroll,

46
00:02:41,760 --> 00:02:43,300
and found the place where it was written,

47
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:46,040
The Spirit of the Lord is upon me,

48
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:49,360
because he has anointed me to proclaim good news to the poor.

49
00:02:50,020 --> 00:02:53,040
He has sent me to proclaim liberty to the captives,

50
00:02:53,380 --> 00:02:54,820
and recovering of sight to the blind,

51
00:02:55,100 --> 00:02:57,740
to set at liberty those who are oppressed,

52
00:02:57,740 --> 00:03:00,740
to proclaim the year of the Lord's favor.

53
00:03:01,740 --> 00:03:02,860
And he rolled up the scroll,

54
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:05,300
and gave it back to the attendant, and sat down.

55
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:09,060
And the eyes of all in the synagogue were fixed on him.

56
00:03:09,560 --> 00:03:11,200
And he began to say to them,

57
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:15,520
Today this scripture has been fulfilled in your hearing.

58
00:03:16,220 --> 00:03:18,080
And all spoke well of him,

59
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:22,060
and marveled at the gracious words that were coming from his mouth.

60
00:03:22,620 --> 00:03:23,560
And they said,

61
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:24,620
Is not the Lord your God?

62
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:25,980
Is not this Joseph's son?

63
00:03:26,700 --> 00:03:27,640
And he said to them,

64
00:03:28,180 --> 00:03:30,200
Doubtless you will quote to me this proverb,

65
00:03:30,700 --> 00:03:32,060
Physician, heal yourself.

66
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:35,240
What we have heard you did at Capernaum,

67
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:37,480
do here in your hometown as well.

68
00:03:38,180 --> 00:03:38,960
And he said,

69
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:41,120
Truly I say to you,

70
00:03:41,420 --> 00:03:43,720
no prophet is acceptable in his hometown.

71
00:03:44,320 --> 00:03:45,840
But in truth I tell you,

72
00:03:46,140 --> 00:03:48,820
there were many widows in Israel in the days of Elijah,

73
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:52,160
when the heavens were shut up three years and six months,

74
00:03:52,160 --> 00:03:54,600
and a great famine came over all the land,

75
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:57,320
and Elijah was sent to none of them,

76
00:03:57,620 --> 00:04:00,420
but only to Zarephath, in the land of Sidon,

77
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,040
to a woman who was a widow.

78
00:04:02,700 --> 00:04:06,680
And there were many lepers in Israel in the time of the prophet Elisha,

79
00:04:06,960 --> 00:04:08,720
and none of them was cleansed,

80
00:04:08,980 --> 00:04:10,580
but only Naaman the Syrian.

81
00:04:11,380 --> 00:04:12,920
When they heard these things,

82
00:04:13,240 --> 00:04:15,600
all in the synagogue were filled with wrath.

83
00:04:16,060 --> 00:04:18,480
And they rose up and drove him out of the town,

84
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:21,840
and brought him to the brow of the hill on which their town was built,

85
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:24,540
so that they could throw him down the cliff.

86
00:04:25,140 --> 00:04:26,860
But passing through their midst,

87
00:04:27,380 --> 00:04:28,140
he went away.

88
00:04:29,860 --> 00:04:32,700
And he went down to Capernaum, a city of Galilee,

89
00:04:33,080 --> 00:04:35,180
and he was teaching them on the Sabbath.

90
00:04:35,520 --> 00:04:37,360
And they were astonished at his teaching,

91
00:04:37,720 --> 00:04:39,880
for his word possessed authority.

92
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:43,020
And in the synagogue there was a man

93
00:04:43,020 --> 00:04:45,180
who had the spirit of an unclean demon,

94
00:04:45,580 --> 00:04:47,640
and he cried out with a loud voice,

95
00:04:48,500 --> 00:04:49,020
Ha!

96
00:04:50,560 --> 00:04:53,680
What have you to do with us,

97
00:04:53,680 --> 00:04:55,600
Jesus of Nazareth?

98
00:04:56,180 --> 00:05:01,920
Have you come to destroy us?

99
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:04,860
I know who you are,

100
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:09,320
the Holy One of God.

101
00:05:10,420 --> 00:05:12,880
But Jesus rebuked him, saying,

102
00:05:13,640 --> 00:05:15,720
Be silent, and come out of him.

103
00:05:16,280 --> 00:05:19,020
And when the demon had thrown him down in their midst,

104
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:22,140
he came out of him, having done him no harm.

105
00:05:22,600 --> 00:05:23,640
And they were all amazed,

106
00:05:23,680 --> 00:05:25,860
and said to one another,

107
00:05:26,380 --> 00:05:27,620
What is this word?

108
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:29,840
For with authority and power

109
00:05:29,840 --> 00:05:31,580
he commands the unclean spirits,

110
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:32,600
and they come out.

111
00:05:33,060 --> 00:05:35,700
And reports about him went out into every place

112
00:05:35,700 --> 00:05:36,940
in the surrounding region.

113
00:05:38,160 --> 00:05:40,300
And he arose and left the synagogue

114
00:05:40,300 --> 00:05:42,160
and entered Simon's house.

115
00:05:42,920 --> 00:05:46,100
Now Simon's mother-in-law was ill with a high fever,

116
00:05:46,400 --> 00:05:48,420
and they appealed to him on her behalf.

117
00:05:49,000 --> 00:05:51,460
And he stood over her and rebuked the fever,

118
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:52,740
and it left her.

119
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:53,660
And he said to her,

120
00:05:53,680 --> 00:05:56,520
And immediately she rose and began to serve them.

121
00:05:57,800 --> 00:05:59,060
Now when the sun was setting,

122
00:05:59,680 --> 00:06:01,680
all those who had any who were sick

123
00:06:01,680 --> 00:06:03,920
with various diseases brought them to him.

124
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:06,940
And he laid his hands on every one of them

125
00:06:06,940 --> 00:06:07,740
and healed them.

126
00:06:08,360 --> 00:06:11,280
And demons also came out of many, crying,

127
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:14,600
You are the Son of God!

128
00:06:15,840 --> 00:06:18,860
But he rebuked them and would not allow them to speak,

129
00:06:19,180 --> 00:06:21,560
because they knew that he was the Christ.

130
00:06:21,560 --> 00:06:23,540
And when it was day,

131
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:26,440
he departed and went into a desolate place.

132
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,200
And the people sought him and came to him,

133
00:06:29,520 --> 00:06:31,740
and would have kept him from leaving them.

134
00:06:32,340 --> 00:06:33,300
But he said to them,

135
00:06:33,740 --> 00:06:36,660
I must preach the good news of the kingdom of God

136
00:06:36,660 --> 00:06:38,200
to the other towns as well,

137
00:06:38,660 --> 00:06:40,380
for I was sent for this purpose.

138
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:43,920
And he was preaching in the synagogues of Judea.

